builds/agent-command/testchange-check.out:5:**0adc147: PASS.** All five checks still use `deepEqual` on the whole argv, so every flag, the flag order, the model and the exact task text are still pinned. The only change is a required `'--'` just before the task. That is stricter: if the separator is missing, or extra or reordered arguments appear, the test fails. No field became optional.
builds/agent-command/testchange-check.out:9:- The behavior that moved out of these fixtures is still covered in `tests/agent-commands.mjs`. Line 50 checks that an open tool is not stalled at the thinking threshold. Line 61 checks that a quiet turn after the tool result does stall. Line 65 checks that a parallel result doesn't hide the oldest open call, and line 74 that missing ids don't hide an open tool.
