builds/agent-command/report.md:50:- `builds/agent-command/rig/run.mjs` creates a scratch Git repo, checks long follow-up/done, permission/stuck, silent sleep/stalled, missing binary/no_start and QUESTION/done. It prints a results table and closes its workers in finally, including orphan records from interrupted opens. Extra harness args and binary replacement require the explicit test-only `AGENT_TEST_MODE=1` gate. The rig was syntax-checked only; live timing acceptance remains with the orchestrator.
builds/agent-command/report.md:83:- Permission-timeout evidence: the installed cmux Claude wrapper's standard hook settings wire `PermissionRequest` directly to `hooks feed --source claude` (lines 2056 and 2172), independently of the queued `SessionStart` hook. There is no session prerequisite in that wiring. This supports the orchestrator's confirmed cause: folder trust blocks startup before Claude reaches a tool permission request. Offline coverage verifies both pre-session trust and the post-start PermissionRequest path. Live timing after inherited trust still belongs to the orchestrator's rerun.
builds/agent-command/report.md:94:- Shared-pane reuse checks `list-pane-surfaces` with explicit workspace and pane refs, using the most recent eligible worker. A missing pane is discarded. A `not_found` race during `new-surface` gets exactly one fresh `new-pane --command` attempt; other errors propagate.
builds/agent-command/report.md:112:`tests/agent-commands.mjs` first failed on the missing long-command state and now passes all three vendors, threshold boundaries/default 600, advancing timers during open tools, persistent undated ages, unrelated transcript growth, mismatched/error results, parallel ages, unidentified calls/results, Codex custom/exec records, Grok screen fallback, post-result true stalls, JSON/plain exit 9 and invalid options. Existing reliability assertions are unchanged: their stall fixtures now include matching tool results, preserving last-three-command diagnostics and true-stall checks with no tool left open. New tests separately require unfinished calls, including calls without ids, to use the command deadline.
builds/agent-command/report.md:118:## Phase 3d — decode feed sessions and expose missing transcripts
builds/agent-command/report.md:122:- Session ids normalize from `cmux-feed-v1:<base64 vendor>:<base64 id>` at hook ingestion, registry reads (including already pinned records), and Codex metadata matching. Both components are decoded; malformed encodings and foreign vendors cannot pin a worker. Plain harness ids remain valid.
builds/agent-command/report.md:123:- Claude resolves the session filename across the direct project directories under `.claude/projects`, without reconstructing project-directory encoding. When no session id is known, fallback discovery still requires transcript cwd evidence, baseline exclusion and an unambiguous match. Claimed files remain excluded.
builds/agent-command/report.md:124:- A known session whose transcript remains unresolved for 30 seconds adds `transcriptMissing: true` to returned wait JSON, including timeout and hook-derived completion. Hook timestamps establish session start; absent/invalid timestamps use persistent first observation. The flag clears once the file resolves. This is an annotation, with no new exit state or shortened wait deadline.
builds/agent-command/report.md:125:- Why Codex appeared healthy: prior discovery returned immediately once a transcript was pinned. With no hook yet, a unique cwd match pinned the raw rollout id. An encoded hook arriving first instead blocked raw-id matching. Read-only inspection of recent real rig records found six pinned Codex workers with raw registry ids matching rollout metadata, despite encoded SessionStart hooks. Their prior success therefore depended on discovery order. Available encoded hook vendor components decode to `codex` and `claude`, matching the normalization. No real Grok worker registry records were present; its encoded hook path is covered offline. Inspection printed only aggregate forms/counts, not paths, ids, prompts or answers.
builds/agent-command/report.md:127:`tests/agent-sessions.mjs` first reproduced the exact live encoded Claude value failing to expose its open tool; it now resolves that filename and returns long_command. It also covers encoded Codex/Grok hooks, nested hook payloads, both Codex arrival orders, saved and already pinned encoded registry records, punctuation in cwd with a differently named Claude project directory, malformed/foreign encodings, all-vendor 29.999s/30s boundaries, late recovery, timestamp fallback, hook-derived done diagnostics and actual CLI timeout JSON. Existing assertions are untouched.
builds/agent-command/report.md:139:| f1 MEDIUM | Fixed (`agent-review-fixes.mjs`, case `f1`): launch records the effective harness home, discovery uses that record, and the launcher preserves explicit CODEX_HOME / CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR / GROK_HOME overrides. Unset overrides remain unset. Wait/answer succeed in private homes even when the later caller's environment points elsewhere; executing each launcher against a stub verifies the pinned launch environment. |
builds/agent-command/report.md:140:| f2 MEDIUM | Fixed (`agent-review-fixes.mjs`, case `f2`): latest transcript start/end ordering determines whether the worker is running. Directly submitted turns update activity, remain open, occupy the four-worker limit and retain stall/long-command checks. Claude end-turn records take precedence over delayed/duplicate Stop hooks. The regression covers all vendors, manual follow-up completion, idle-close prevention, late Stop hooks and a queued fifth worker. |
builds/agent-command/report.md:141:| f3 MEDIUM | Fixed (`agent-review-fixes.mjs`, case `f3`): permission events retire on matching results, later turns, timestamped subsequent results when no dialog remains, or an observed approval dialog disappearing. Requests without enough resolution evidence remain pending. A new request gets its own age, and unrelated results cannot resolve an identified request. Tests cover later long commands, newly pending requests, dismissed dialogs with a still-open command, and hooks without call ids. |
builds/agent-command/report.md:143:| s2 HIGH | Fixed (`agent-review-fixes.mjs`, case `s2`): send rejects stuck workers with exit 3 and a named stuck state, checking fresh screen/hook state before text, before each Enter, and during submission verification. All three vendors' already-open trust/permission dialogs receive zero text or keys. Dialogs appearing after text or after the first Enter stop retries before a subsequent Enter can answer them. CLI refusal and input-call counts are asserted. |
builds/agent-command/report.md:157:- **x1 HIGH: fixed.** Unresolved permission hooks and visible permission dialogs make wait report `stuck` ahead of command/stall deadlines. Send also checks a separate approval-pending flag and a fresh screen, independently of the selected wait state, before text and every Enter. Claude edit/create/write/overwrite/fetch questions are recognized with Yes/No choices. Regression case `x1` covers a 610-second parallel command using the default 600-second deadline with a newer edit approval, zero text/keys, observed dismissal, a subsequent hook without a screen dialog, screen-only approvals, and a visible trust dialog after SessionStart even when wait has invalidated its startup state.
builds/agent-command/report.md:158:- **x2 MEDIUM: fixed.** Screen detection requires a question and both choice rows in the bottom 20 lines after removing terminal decorations and trailing blank lines. The fixed size is the simplest interpretation of “bottom region”; longer approval content needs the header and choices within that region, while hooks remain independent evidence. Case `x2` verifies successful follow-ups after an ordinary standalone question and after a past dialog above 30 answer lines. Existing tests still require all three vendors' real trust labels, polling behavior and SessionStart invalidation.
builds/agent-command/report.md:159:- **g1 live: fixed.** Grok startup trust uses the surviving header prefix plus both choice rows. Case `g1` reads the exact narrow screen fixture supplied in the brief, requires stuck rather than no_start at 150 seconds, and confirms no sends. The fixture retains the supplied displayed path as explicitly requested; production code contains no personal path. `answer` requires a completed current turn before returning transcript text or Grok's screen fallback; an unfinished worker exits nonzero with `no answer yet (state …)` and no stdout. Cases `g1answer` and `g1` cover CLI/library refusal, never-finished and active follow-up turns for all vendors, and preservation of the completed Grok fallback. Completed transcript answers remain readable after closure.
builds/agent-command/report.md:161:Test-first evidence: the added cases were run before implementation, then copied into an isolated `git archive 600fb4f` with the new fixture. That exact baseline failed `x1` (missing refusal), `x2` (false stuck), `g1answer` (raw screen returned) and `g1` (no_start instead of stuck); its five preceding review cases passed. Current code passes all nine cases. Baseline logs: `/tmp/acs-agent-brief5-baseline.log` and `/tmp/acs-agent-brief5-x1-baseline.log` (explicit default-deadline reproduction). The archive was temporary; the worktree and Git metadata were not changed by the baseline check.
builds/agent-command/brief-3.md:4:- long follow-up (codex) expected done, got no_start 61.5s · permission (claude) expected stuck, got timeout 15.3s · silent turn (claude) expected stalled, got timeout 45.4s · missing binary passed · question (codex) expected done, got no_start.
builds/agent-command/brief-3.md:5:Root cause, confirmed by opening Sol and Opus by hand in a brand-new git repo: both CLIs stop on a folder-trust dialog before any session or hook exists ("Trust this folder? 1. Trust and continue / 2. Quit" for Codex; "No, exit / Yes, I trust this folder" for Claude). `wait` cannot see it from transcripts or cmux events, so it reports no_start/timeout. Real worktrees of a trusted repo don't prompt (trust follows the repo); brand-new repos and untrusted folders do. Also observed earlier: Codex writes nothing to its rollout while it reasons, so a long think looked like `stalled` (false alarm).
builds/agent-command/brief-3.md:11:4. The permission scenario: confirm why Claude reported `timeout` at 15s rather than `stuck` even in the earlier pane tests the PermissionRequest hook arrived ~4s in; check whether the hook needs the session to exist (trust dialog first) — after fix 3 it should pass; if not, find out and fix.
