builds/agent-command/fable.out:69:- **Interactive panes can stall** on a permission prompt nobody sees. Launch with explicit sandbox and approval flags, and watch for `agent.hook.Notification`.
builds/agent-command/brief-2.md:25:Add builds/agent-command/rig/run.mjs (not shipped) that, in a scratch git repo it creates under $TMPDIR, uses the real `agent` command to provoke each failure and asserts the right `wait` state within the stated time: (a) a long message to Codex → must be `done`, never silently `unsent`; (b) a Claude worker started with `--permission-mode default` told to run a shell command → `stuck` within 15s; (c) a worker told to run `sleep 600` with `--stall-after 30` → `stalled` within 45s (b and c use a test-only `--launch-extra` / env hook you add for the rig, documented as test-only); (d) a launcher pointed at a missing binary → `no_start` within 75s; (e) a worker ending with `QUESTION: …` → `done` with question. It prints a table: scenario, harness, expected, got, seconds, pass/fail, and closes every pane it opened. Do not run it — the orchestrator will.
