builds/agent-command/fixcheck.out:1243:++- `builds/agent-command/rig/run.mjs` creates a scratch Git repo, checks long follow-up/done, permission/stuck, silent sleep/stalled, missing binary/no_start and QUESTION/done. It prints a results table and closes its workers in finally, including orphan records from interrupted opens. Extra harness args and binary replacement require the explicit test-only `AGENT_TEST_MODE=1` gate. The rig was syntax-checked only; live timing acceptance remains with the orchestrator.
builds/agent-command/fixcheck.out:1276:++- Permission-timeout evidence: the installed cmux Claude wrapper's standard hook settings wire `PermissionRequest` directly to `hooks feed --source claude` (lines 2056 and 2172), independently of the queued `SessionStart` hook. There is no session prerequisite in that wiring. This supports the orchestrator's confirmed cause: folder trust blocks startup before Claude reaches a tool permission request. Offline coverage verifies both pre-session trust and the post-start PermissionRequest path. Live timing after inherited trust still belongs to the orchestrator's rerun.
builds/agent-command/fixcheck.out:1287:++- Shared-pane reuse checks `list-pane-surfaces` with explicit workspace and pane refs, using the most recent eligible worker. A missing pane is discarded. A `not_found` race during `new-surface` gets exactly one fresh `new-pane --command` attempt; other errors propagate.
builds/agent-command/fixcheck.out:1305:++`tests/agent-commands.mjs` first failed on the missing long-command state and now passes all three vendors, threshold boundaries/default 600, advancing timers during open tools, persistent undated ages, unrelated transcript growth, mismatched/error results, parallel ages, unidentified calls/results, Codex custom/exec records, Grok screen fallback, post-result true stalls, JSON/plain exit 9 and invalid options. Existing reliability assertions are unchanged: their stall fixtures now include matching tool results, preserving last-three-command diagnostics and true-stall checks with no tool left open. New tests separately require unfinished calls, including calls without ids, to use the command deadline.
builds/agent-command/fixcheck.out:1311:++## Phase 3d — decode feed sessions and expose missing transcripts
builds/agent-command/fixcheck.out:1315:++- Session ids normalize from `cmux-feed-v1:<base64 vendor>:<base64 id>` at hook ingestion, registry reads (including already pinned records), and Codex metadata matching. Both components are decoded; malformed encodings and foreign vendors cannot pin a worker. Plain harness ids remain valid.
builds/agent-command/fixcheck.out:1316:++- Claude resolves the session filename across the direct project directories under `.claude/projects`, without reconstructing project-directory encoding. When no session id is known, fallback discovery still requires transcript cwd evidence, baseline exclusion and an unambiguous match. Claimed files remain excluded.
builds/agent-command/fixcheck.out:1317:++- A known session whose transcript remains unresolved for 30 seconds adds `transcriptMissing: true` to returned wait JSON, including timeout and hook-derived completion. Hook timestamps establish session start; absent/invalid timestamps use persistent first observation. The flag clears once the file resolves. This is an annotation, with no new exit state or shortened wait deadline.
builds/agent-command/fixcheck.out:1318:++- Why Codex appeared healthy: prior discovery returned immediately once a transcript was pinned. With no hook yet, a unique cwd match pinned the raw rollout id. An encoded hook arriving first instead blocked raw-id matching. Read-only inspection of recent real rig records found six pinned Codex workers with raw registry ids matching rollout metadata, despite encoded SessionStart hooks. Their prior success therefore depended on discovery order. Available encoded hook vendor components decode to `codex` and `claude`, matching the normalization. No real Grok worker registry records were present; its encoded hook path is covered offline. Inspection printed only aggregate forms/counts, not paths, ids, prompts or answers.
builds/agent-command/fixcheck.out:1320:++`tests/agent-sessions.mjs` first reproduced the exact live encoded Claude value failing to expose its open tool; it now resolves that filename and returns long_command. It also covers encoded Codex/Grok hooks, nested hook payloads, both Codex arrival orders, saved and already pinned encoded registry records, punctuation in cwd with a differently named Claude project directory, malformed/foreign encodings, all-vendor 29.999s/30s boundaries, late recovery, timestamp fallback, hook-derived done diagnostics and actual CLI timeout JSON. Existing assertions are untouched.
